Visualization 2


Show the code
# Select movies with known release years
covid_titles &lt;- netflix_titles |&gt;
    filter(!is.na(title),!is.na(release_year)) |&gt;
    mutate(period = ifelse(release_year &lt;= 2019, "Before COVID-19 (2019 and earlier)", "During COVID-19 (2020)")) |&gt;

    mutate(disease = str_detect(str_to_lower(title), "\\b(covid|coronavirus|virus|viral|pandemic|epidemic|infection|infected|infectious|disease|plague|outbreak|fever|sick|sickness|illness|ill|contagion|contagious|germ|symptom|cough|flu|influenza|bacteria|bacterial|vaccine|vaccination|quarantine|inject|injection|shot|hospital|nurse|doctor)\\b"))|&gt;

    mutate(death = str_detect(str_to_lower(title),"\\b(death|dead|dying|die|died|dies|funeral|grave|graveyard|morgue|corpse|cemetery|burial|bury|buried|murder|murdered|killer|kill|killed|suicide|fatal|fatality|blood|bloody)\\b")) |&gt;

    mutate(isolation = str_detect(str_to_lower(title),"\\b(alone|lonely|loneliness|isolation|isolated|quarantine|lockdown|trapped|confined|separated|solitude|abandoned|stranded|deserted|hidden|missing|escape|prison|captive|imprisoned|locked|room|cabin|shelter|exile|outsider|cage|lone|lock)\\b")) |&gt;

    mutate(fear_survival = str_detect(str_to_lower(title),"\\b(fear|afraid|terror|terrified|panic|nightmare|survive|survival|survivor|apocalypse|apocalyptic|disaster|catastrophe|danger|threat|warning|destruction|collapse|end|extinction|invasion|attack|crisis|emergency|sacrifice|shelter|escape|chaos|doom|doomed|scared|panic|petrify)\\b"))



#converting the four theme columns into rows
covid_word_counts &lt;- covid_titles |&gt;
    pivot_longer(cols = c(disease, death, isolation, fear_survival), names_to = "theme",values_to = "contains_word") |&gt;
    group_by(period, theme) |&gt;
    summarize(titles_with_words = sum(contains_word))

#counting all movies in each period
period_totals &lt;- covid_titles |&gt;
    group_by(period) |&gt;
    summarize(total_titles = length(show_id))

#calculating the percentage of movies within each year category containing each theme
covid_word_counts &lt;- covid_word_counts |&gt;
    left_join(period_totals, by = "period") |&gt;
    mutate(percentage = titles_with_words / total_titles * 100,
           theme = ifelse(theme == "disease", "Disease & Illness", ifelse(theme == "death", "Death", ifelse(theme == "isolation", "Isolation & Loneliness", "Fear, Survival, & Disaster")))
          )

#making the plot
ggplot(covid_word_counts, aes(x = theme, y = percentage, fill = period)) + 
    geom_col(position = "dodge") +
    labs(
        title = "Pandemic-Related Vocabulary in Netflix Movie & TV Show Titles",
        subtitle = "Comparing titles released before and during COVID-19",
        x = "Vocabulary theme",
        y = "Movies/TV shows containing at least one matching word (%)",
        fill = "Release period",
    ) +
    theme_minimal() +
    theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 20, hjust = 1))









For the second visual, I wanted to see if there was a difference in the types of words in titles before and during Covid-19. Thus, I created four categories of pandemic-related words: words surrounding death, words about diseases, words corresponding with fear, survival, and disaster, and finally, words associated with being isolated. Movies/TV shows that were released in 2019 or before, I classified as “Before Covid”, and any movies/shows released from 2020 were considered “During Covid” titles. Each bar chart on this visual represents the percentage of titles within each time period that have words that fit in each of these categories.
From the visual, we can see that there was a bit of a spike in the percentage of movie/show titles that contained words associated with death during Covid. Specifically, around 1.75% of all movies released before 2019 contained words associated with death, while around 3.2% of movies released in 2020 had titles with words related to death. There is also an increase in the percentage of movie/show titles that contained words associated with disease during Covid, with around 0.10% of titles containing words associated with illness before 2019 and around 0.70% of titles containing these types of words during Covid. However, the other two categories do not show a significant increase in percentage of titles containing these words between the two time periods, with the percentage of titles containing isolation and fear/survival themes actually decreasing between before and during Covid.
While it’s possible Covid could have influenced this increase, we cannot determine causality from this bar chart. First, what people classify as pandemic-related vocabulary is subjective, and I only included a handful of words that I personally thought would fit in the pandemic/health/death theme. Also, this dataset only includes titles released in 2020 and before, meaning the “before Covid” category has a much larger number of movies that could match the groups than the “during Covid” group does. Therefore, while the bar chart does show us that movies and shows during Covid have a higher percentage of pandemic-related words, we cannot establish causality between COVID-19 and any changes in movie/show titles.
